hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24309","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: Ali said to me: Ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a man who fondles his wife and madhy comes out of him without the water of life, for were it not that his daughter is under me I would have asked him, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man fondles his wife and madhy comes out of him without the water of life, he said: He washes his private part and performs ablution as for prayer."
"24310","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: I and two companions of mine came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and severe hunger befell us, so we presented ourselves to the people and no one hosted us, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took us to his dwelling, and with him were four goats, and he said to me: O Miqdad, divide their milk among us in quarters, so I used to divide it among us in quarters, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was detained one night, so I said to myself that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had gone to some of the Ansar and eaten until full and drunk until quenched, so if only I drank his share, and I kept on until I went to his share and drank it, then I covered the cup, and when I finished I was seized by regret for past and present, and I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, will come hungry and find nothing, so I covered myself and kept talking to myself, and while I was so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered and greeted with a greeting that the awake could hear and the sleeper would not wake, then he came to the cup and uncovered it and saw nothing, and said: O Allah, feed whoever feeds me and give drink to whoever gives me drink, and I seized the supplication, so I went to the knife and took it, then I went to the goats and began feeling which was fattest, and my hand would not pass over the udder of one but I found it full, so I milked until I filled the cup, then I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah, so he raised his head to me and said: Some of your misdeeds, O Miqdad, what is the news, I said: Drink, then the news, so he drank until quenched, then handed it to me and I drank, and he said: What is the news, so I told him, and he said: This is a blessing sent down from heaven, why did you not tell me so we could give our two companions to drink, so I said: When the blessing has reached me and you, I do not care whom it misses."
"24311","Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father, who said: We sat with al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad one day, and a man passed by him and said: Blessed are these two eyes which saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by Allah we wish we had seen what you saw and witnessed what you witnessed, so he became angry, and I was amazed, for he had said nothing but good, then he turned to him and said: What makes a man wish for a presence which Allah kept him away from, he does not know how he would have been in it, by Allah, peoples attended the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whom Allah threw on their nostrils into Hell, they did not answer him nor believe him, do you not praise Allah that He brought you out knowing none but your Lord, believing in what your Prophet brought, spared the trial through others, by Allah, Allah sent the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the severest state in which a prophet among the prophets was sent, in a period of ignorance, they saw no religion better than worship of idols, so he came with a criterion by which he separated truth from falsehood, and separated between father and his son, until a man would see his father or his son or his brother a disbeliever, while Allah had opened the lock of his heart to faith, knowing that if he perished he would enter the Fire, so his eye would not be cooled while knowing his beloved is in the Fire, and it is that about which He, mighty and majestic, said: Those who say: Our Lord, grant us from our spouses and offspring comfort of eyes."
"24312","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from al-Miqdad ibn Amr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if a man strikes me with the sword and cuts off my hand, then seeks refuge from me by a tree, then says: There is no god but Allah, shall I kill him, he said: No, so I repeated twice or thrice, and he said: No, unless you become like him before he said what he said, and he becomes like you before you did what you did."
"24313","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Miqdad, who said: I and two companions of mine came, our hearing and sight gone from hardship, and we began offering ourselves to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and no one would accept us, so we went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he took us to his family, and there were three goats, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Milk this milk among us, so we used to milk, and each person would drink his share, and we would set aside for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, his share, and he would come at night and greet with a greeting that would not wake the sleeper but the awake could hear, then he would go to the mosque and pray, then come to his drink and drink it, and Satan came to me one night and said: Muhammad goes to the Ansar and they gift him and he gets with them what he needs, he has no need of this sip, so drink it, and he kept adorning it to me until I drank it, and when it settled in my belly and he knew there was no way to it, he made me regret, saying: Woe to you, what have you done, you drank the drink of Muhammad, he will come and not see it and supplicate against you and perish, and your world and hereafter go, and upon me was a woolen wrap, whenever I raised it over my head my feet showed, and when I let it down over my feet my head showed, and sleep would not come to me, and as for my two companions, they slept, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and greeted as he used to greet, then went to the mosque and prayed, then came to his drink and uncovered it and found nothing in it, and raised his head to the sky, I said: Now he will supplicate against me and perish, but he said: O Allah, feed whoever feeds me and give drink to whoever gives me drink, so I went to the wrap and tied it on, and took the knife and went to the goats feeling which was fattest to slaughter for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they were all full, so I went to a vessel of the family of Muhammad which they had not hoped to milk into, and Abu al-Nadr once said: to milk into, and I milked into it until foam rose over it, then I brought it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Have you not drunk your drink tonight, O Miqdad, I said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah, so he drank then handed to me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, drink, so he drank then handed to me, and I took what remained and drank, and when I knew the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was quenched and his supplication had reached me, I laughed until I fell to the ground, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One of your misdeeds, O Miqdad, I said: O Messenger of Allah, such and such happened, I did so and so, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This was but a mercy from Allah, why did you not tell me, we would wake these two companions of yours to get some of it, I said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I do not care, when I got it and got it with you, who among the people got it."
"24314","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, Sulaym ibn Amir narrated to me, al-Miqdad, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to me, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When the Day of Resurrection comes, the sun will be brought near to the servants until it is a mile or two away, and the sun will melt them, and they will be in sweat according to their deeds, some taken up to their heels, some to their knees, some to their waists, and some bridled with it as with a bridle."
"24315","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Jabir narrated to me, who said: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir say: I heard al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There will not remain on the face of the earth a house of mud-brick nor of hair but Allah will enter into it the word of Islam, with the might of one mighty or the humiliation of one humbled, either Allah, mighty and majestic, honors them and makes them of its people, or humbles them and they submit to it."
"24316","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to me, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr and Amr ibn al-Aswad, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad and Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the ruler seeks suspicion among the people, he corrupts them."
"24317","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Sulaym narrated to us, who said: Al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad said: I do not say good nor evil about a man until I see how he is sealed, meaning after something I heard from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, it was said: And what did you hear, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The heart of the son of Adam turns over more violently than a cooking pot when it boils together."
"24318","Ya'qub narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, then al-Junda'i, informed me, that Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him, that al-Miqdad ibn Amr al-Kindi, who was an ally of Banu Zuhrah and was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed him, that he said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What if I meet a man of the disbelievers and we fight, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it, then seeks refuge from me by a tree and says: I submit to Allah, shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he says it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not kill him, he said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands then said that after cutting it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not kill him, for he is in your station before you kill him, and you are in his station before he says the word he said."
"24319","Ya'qub narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, then al-Junda'i, informed me, that Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him, that al-Miqdad ibn Amr al-Kindi, who was an ally of Banu Zuhrah and was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed him, that he said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What if I meet a man of the disbelievers and we fight, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it, then seeks refuge from me by a tree and says: I submit to Allah, shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he says it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not kill him, he said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands then said that after cutting it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not kill him, for he is in your station before you kill him, and you are in his station before he says the word he said."
"24320","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a man who comes close to his wife and emits madhy, he said: If one of you finds that, let him sprinkle his private part, meaning wash it, and perform ablution as for prayer."
"24321","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah al-Walid ibn Kamil, of the people of Hims, al-Bajali, narrated to us, al-Muhallab ibn Hujr al-Bahrani narrated to me, from Duba'ah bint al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, from her father, that he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray toward a pillar or a stick or a tree but he placed it at his right or left eyebrow-side, and he would not face it directly."
"24322","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Kamil narrated to me, from al-Hujr, or from Abu al-Hujr ibn al-Muhallab al-Bahrani, who said: Dubay'ah bint al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib narrated to me, from her father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prayed toward a pillar or a piece of wood or the like, would not place it in front of his eyes, but would place it at his left eyebrow-side."
"24323","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: I came to Madinah, I and a companion of mine, and we presented ourselves to the people and no one hosted us, so we came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him, and he took us to his dwelling, and with him were four goats, and he said: Milk them, O Miqdad, and divide them into four portions, and give each person his portion, so I used to do that, and I set aside for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, his portion one night, then he was detained, and I lay on my bed, and my soul said to me: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has gone to a household of the Ansar, so if you got up and drank this drink, and it kept at me until I got up and drank his portion, and when it entered my belly and settled, I was seized by regret for past and present, and I said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, will come hungry and thirsty and see nothing in the cup, so I covered my face with a garment, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and greeted with a greeting that the awake could hear and the sleeper would not wake, and uncovered it and saw nothing, and raised his head to the sky and said: O Allah, give drink to whoever gave me drink and feed whoever fed me, so I seized his supplication, and got up and took the knife and went to the goats, feeling which was fattest to slaughter it, and my hand fell on the udder of one of them and it was full, and I looked at another and it was full, and I looked at all of them and they were full, so I milked into the vessel and brought it to him and said: Drink, so he said: The news, O Miqdad, so I said: Drink, then the news, so he said: Some of your misdeeds, O Miqdad, so he drank then said: Drink, so I said: Drink, O Prophet of Allah, so he drank until his sides were filled, then I took it and drank, then I told him the news, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hah, so I said: Such and such happened, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This is a blessing sent down from heaven, why did you not tell me so I could give your two companions to drink, so I said: When I drink the blessing, I and you, I do not care whom it misses."
"24324","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, who said: He began praising a governor of Uthman, so al-Miqdad went and began throwing dust in his face, so Uthman said to him: What is this, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you see those who praise extravagantly, throw dust in their faces."
"24325","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that Sa'id ibn al-As sent a delegation from Iraq to Uthman, and they came praising him, so al-Miqdad began throwing dust in their faces, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to throw dust in the faces of those who praise extravagantly, and Sufyan once said: So al-Miqdad stood and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Throw dust in the faces of those who praise extravagantly, al-Zubayr said: As for al-Miqdad, he has done what was upon him."
"24326","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ata narrated to us, from Ayish ibn Anas al-Bakri, who said: Ali, Ammar, and al-Miqdad discussed madhy, so Ali said: I am a man who emits much madhy, and I am shy to ask him because his daughter is under me, so he said to one of them, to Ammar or to al-Miqdad, Ata said: Ayish named him to me and I forgot him: Ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I asked him, and he said: That is madhy, let him wash that from himself, I said: What is that from himself, he said: His organ, and let him perform ablution well, or perform ablution like his ablution for prayer, and sprinkle in his private part, or his private part."
"24327","Yahya narrated to us, from Wa'il ibn Dawud, who said: I heard Abdullah al-Bahi, that a party stopped at Uthman ibn Affan and praised him and lauded him, and there was al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, so he took a handful of earth and threw it in the faces of the party, and said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you hear those who praise extravagantly, throw dust in their faces."
"24328","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, who said: A man came to Uthman and praised him to his face, so al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad began throwing dust in his face, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us, when we meet those who praise extravagantly, to throw dust in their faces."
"24329","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, who said: A man stood praising a commander among the commanders, so al-Miqdad began throwing dust in his face, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to throw dust in the faces of those who praise extravagantly."
"24330","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abu al-Nadr, the freedman of Umar ibn Ubaydullah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, that Ali ibn Abi Talib ordered him to ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a man when he comes close to his wife and madhy comes out of him, what is upon him, Ali said: For with me is the daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I am shy to ask him, al-Miqdad said: So I asked the Messenger of Allah about that, and he said: If one of you finds that, let him sprinkle his private part and perform ablution as for prayer."
"24331","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj, Shu'bah informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, that a man began praising Uthman, then he mentioned the like of the meaning of the hadith of Sufyan."
"24332","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, that he said: He informed me that al-Miqdad informed him, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I meet a man of the disbelievers and he fights me, and we exchange two blows, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it, then seeks refuge from me by a tree and says: I submit to Allah, shall I fight him, O Messenger of Allah, after he says it, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not kill him, I said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands then said that after cutting it, shall I fight him, so the Messenger of Allah said: Do not kill him, for if you kill him, he is in your station before you kill him, and you are in his station before he says the word he said."
"24333","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, that al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad narrated to him, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I and a man differ, then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: Shall I kill him or leave him."
